  "root_node": "source.raw.customer",
  "cause": "upstream_data",
  "action": "escalate",
  "evidence": "The model stg_customers failed contract validation because its column account_balance is defined as VARCHAR, but the staging contract expects DECIMAL(15,2). The source column raw.customer.c_acctbal is VARCHAR. Profiling shows the conversion to DECIMAL(15,2) is not lossless: values have at most 1 decimal place, so converting would lose precision and cannot be recovered. According to policy, type changes are only patched if lossless, otherwise the issue must be escalated to the source owner. The problem originates in the raw.customer source table."
}
